From eb533bd6ad03995f88fb01e429fa6ab03e73ba10 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 09:08:45 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] test: characterization goldens for wire, composition, routes
 and refusals

Four new suites under src/__tests__/golden/, written on today's code with
the test kit and frozen from here (gate 10): C2 wire (55 tests) pins every
request the pages send, whole (URL, method, headers, the raw body with its
key order, the poll after): the pane's gestures at the player's, the
Gamemaster's and a companion's seat, each send of useTableRolls, End Turn
and Undo, the party take, the table, journal, party, companion and cookbook
polls with their backoff, chat read, and the server's command and views of
a held roll as JSON. C3 composition (7) pins which area root renders which
and the props it hands down, read from the fiber tree (retired in commit
26). C5 routes (141) calls every route method over the real db modules on
prismaFake rows, signed out, another's sheet, each seat and the happy path,
with every header, the body text and the Prisma calls in order, the
module's events and commands, the cookbook, and the pages' titles,
not-found and sign-in paths. C6 refusals (243) pins the issues of every
schema, each event's read or prettified refusal, and each body route's
415, 413 and 400.

Snapshots were written once with --ci=false over these four files only;
the suites then pass with --ci, alone and together (446 tests, 454
snapshots), eslint prints nothing for them and tsc is clean. Mutation
spot-checks, each reverted: a body key's order (spend: count before
counter) fails C2's "each command at the player seat"; CompanionPane's
sharedDice made false fails C3's "CompanionPane"; markBridgePolled no
longer setting lastSeenAt fails C5's "commands POST, cold"; an issue's
words ("Only an attack has a target") fail C6's "refuses dice the roll
does not throw".

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
